erence is\n\n$$\nA-B={1,3,12}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67e90c94-5018-582f-8692-a1155f41f7c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Differences of Sets Given Verbally"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a9bf1c3-c25e-546d-bf50-f506b6cb2bee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4,8,16,20,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296501} {:answer/id #uuid "fb5b5b4e-290f-541c-ba2f-6ba2982c59cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{12,24…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296502} {:answer/id #uuid "d4685bed-f4c4-5ce4-b803-08ec3f7b9daa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3,6,9,15,18,21,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296503} {:answer/id #uuid "4a3343f8-3a82-58af-bc78-065391a8604e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3,4,6,8,9,15,16,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296504} {:answer/id #uuid "0db51cb2-8bf8-5b33-a63b-bc763b47289f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,3,6,9,15,18,21,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a9bf1c3-c25e-546d-bf50-f506b6cb2bee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4,8,16,20,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296501} :answer-field/id #uuid "af625279-b9b8-5e8b-9297-c5d5fbef4f97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4c54f56-ff83-5c5e-b062-1e1004f84f48" :question/math-academy-id "q-81766" :question/problem "Let $A$  be the set of all multiples of $3$ greater than $0$ and let $B$  be the set of all multiples of $4$ greater than $0.$ What is $B-A?$" :question/worked-solution "The multiples of $3$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA={3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB={4,8,12,16,20,24,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $B-A$ is the *difference* of $B$ and $A,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $B$ but *not* in $A.$\n\nThe elements of $B$ that are also in $A$ are $12,24,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $12$). So, we must remove these elements from $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-A & ={4,8,12,16,20,24,…}-{3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…} \\\\  & ={4,8,16,20,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296506 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4687dcd7-a5ab-5dc6-be6d-89d806a61a02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d916ceaf-2ba5-51f1-a52e-7283f47b312b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a,b,c,d,e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296508} {:answer/id #uuid "ce9fe0e8-4cd9-5f96-b15d-2574434f9775" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{c,e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296509} {:answer/id #uuid "cf300eda-a1f8-59bd-9992-7e9646dfb4e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{d}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296510} {:answer/id #uuid "6aac7f1a-9eff-50cf-848b-752667e08cac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a,b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296511} {:answer/id #uuid "d854b98c-8a77-5a8b-a783-415c746d5652" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a,b,c,e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6aac7f1a-9eff-50cf-848b-752667e08cac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a,b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296511} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e3ab4dc-0b5f-5446-b5e8-6d38cdb8c5ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c0d693f2-85f9-5df3-8dc0-db913e9cad2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-86703" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/15f7165e2528c93766591e246ce971b4fc72277d03374bd78b5a3e57f302bdb3.png)\n\nGiven the sets $S={a,b,d}$ and $T={c,d,e},$ find $S-T.$" :question/worked-solution "The difference $S-T$ consists of all the elements that are in $S$ but not $T.$ To represent $S-T,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $S$ but not $T.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/c3694dbc8f5eb9bdaf352fc3d456c6dabc07224f18e73257a9030000e5b1263e.png)\n\nThe elements $a$ and $b$ are in $S$ but not $T.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nS-T={a,b}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67e90c94-5018-582f-8692-a1155f41f7c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Differences of Sets Given Verbally"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ecf4f13-46a7-5a48-8781-3e8aa487b4f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296515} {:answer/id #uuid "d570f2dc-feb9-5b76-8a34-e27c0daa2db7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296516} {:answer/id #uuid "cd0e9672-9b63-5d8a-89f7-7848589f0b62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2,4,8,16,32,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296517} {:answer/id #uuid "5af50fb6-4ecf-5b53-b877-067f72197875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3,9,27,81,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296518} {:answer/id #uuid "43368a1c-ade4-511d-afc7-94d932fc4510" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,2,4,8,16,32,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd0e9672-9b63-5d8a-89f7-7848589f0b62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2,4,8,16,32,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296517} :answer-field/id #uuid "64e0a480-4f13-59b7-a55d-6b4ac38114fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296514}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "75546b77-28ba-5102-9034-ab09a7671149" :question/math-academy-id "q-86704" :question/problem "Let $X$  be the set of all non-negative integer powers of $2$ and let $Y$  be the set of all non-negative integer powers of $3.$  What is $X-Y?$" :question/worked-solution "The powers of $2$ that are greater or equal to $1$ are\n\n$$\nX={1,2,4,8,16,32,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, the powers of $3$ that are greater or equal to $1$ are\n\n$$\nY={1,3,9,27,81,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $X-Y$ is the *difference* of $X$ and $Y,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $X$ but *not* in $Y.$\n\nThe only element of $X$ that are also in $Y$ is $1.$ So, we must remove this element from $X.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X-Y & ={1,2,4,8,16,32,…}-{1,3,9,27,81,…} \\\\  & ={2,4,8,16,32,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
